==Trivia==
*The word ''phantasmagoria'' can refer to a dreamlike sequence of surreal imagery that is constantly shifting or a [[wikipedia:Phantasmagoria|form of horror theatre]] that used [[wikipedia:Magic lantern|magic lanterns]] to project monsters before the audience.
*The 幻想郷 ''Gensōkyō'' part of Phantasmagoria's Japanese name (マジカ幻想郷 ''Majika Gensōkyō'', "Magica Land of Fantasy") means "Land of Fantasy" or "Land of Illusion", but is also the name of the [https://en.touhouwiki.net/wiki/Gensokyo setting] of the ''[[wikipedia:Touhou Project|Touhou Project]]'' series.
**Its English name also appears to reference some games in the ''Touhou Project'' series, namely the third, ''[https://en.touhouwiki.net/wiki/Phantasmagoria_of_Dim.Dream Phantasmagoria of Dimensional Dream]'', and the ninth, ''[https://en.touhouwiki.net/wiki/Phantasmagoria_of_Dim.Dream Phantasmagoria of Flower View]''.
*Each stage of Phantasmagoria is named after a different mythical creature, though some of them are not referred to directly:
**[[Taurus Trail]] (タウロス街道, Taurosu Kaidō, "Taurus Highway") is named after the [[wikipedia:Minotaur|Minotaur]] (ミノタウロス ''Minotaurosu'') or [[wikipedia:Centaur|centaur]] (ケンタウロス ''kentaurosu''). This could be a subtle reference to [[Labyrinth of Hades]], another stage with [[Doge Dark]], [[Kory]] and [[Bun Bun Black]], as the Minotaur is contained within the [[wikipedia:Labyrinth|Labyrinth]] in Greek mythology.
**[[Undead City]]'s Japanese name (不死街 ''Fushi-chō'', "Immortal Town") is a pun on 不死鳥 ''fushichō'' ([[wikipedia:Phoenix (mythology)|phoenix]]) and 街 ''chō'' (town). Like a phoenix, the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] in the stage can come back to life.
**[[Drag-Inn]] is a pun on ''dragon''.
*The many [[Sir Seal|seals]] in [[Mermaid Lounge]] may be a reference to the theory that mermaid myths originated from sightings of marine mammals such as manatees, dugongs or seals.
**They might also represent the [[wikipedia:Selkie|selkie]], a mythical creature that can switch between human and seal forms, as selkies are occasionally confused with mermaids.
*Phantasmagoria is the first sub-chapter since [[Singularityville]] to only contain one word in its name.

